 "notes": "The Ulysses (95 m, 1887) on the north face of Gubal Seghir and the Barge (about 35 x 6 m) in the sheltered bay south-west of the Bluff Point light. Island shore, reef edge, light and both wreck positions come from OpenStreetMap; dimensions and depths from the Red Sea Wreck Project (Ulysses bow 4-5 m, propeller 28 m; Barge 14 m). No published heading exists for either wreck: the Ulysses is drawn bow into the reef running straight down the slope, the Barge along the reef edge, and the engine and hold depths are interpolated. The drift runs from the wreck with the current along the reef; positions are approximate.",
